card.statement:
Let $(A,m,\eta,L,\mu,\alpha,\beta)$ be a Lie-Rinehart monoid in $\calC$. Let $(\mathfrak{L},\mathfrak{u})$ be another Lie monoid in $\calC$. A morphism $\mathcal{H}: L \rightarrow \mathfrak{L}\otimes A$ is called a crossed homomorphism if it satisfies the following axiom:

\begin{equation*}
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0.25, 0.5) -- (0.25, 1)--(0,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.5, 0) -- (0.25, 0.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.5, 1.5) -- (0.25, 1);
\btoken{0.25, 1}{west}{\mathcal{H}};
\btoken{0.25, 0.5}{west}{\mu};
\end{tikzpicture} \ = \
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0, 1) -- (0.25, 1.25)--(0.25,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.25, 0) --(0.25,0.25)-- (-0.25, 0.75) -- (-0.25, 1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.25, 0.25) -- (0.5, 0.5) -- (0.5, 1)--(0.25,1.25);
\btoken{0.25, 1.25}{west}{\alpha};
\btoken{0.25, 0.25}{west}{\mathcal{H}};
\end{tikzpicture}\ - \
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0, 0.25) -- (-0.25, 0.5)--(-0.25,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0, 0.25) -- (0.5, 0.75) -- (0.5, 1)--(0.25,1.25)--(0.25,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.5, 0) -- (0.5, 0.25) -- (0, 0.75)--(0,1)--(0.25,1.25);
\btoken{0.25, 1.25}{west}{\alpha};
\btoken{0, 0.25}{east}{\mathcal{H}};
\end{tikzpicture} \ + \
\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]
\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0, 0.25) -- (-0.25, 0.5)--(-0.25,1)--(0,1.25)--(0,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0, 0.25) -- (0.75,1.25)--(0.75,1.5);
\draw[bmod] (0.75, 0.25) -- (1, 0.5) -- (1, 1)--(0.75,1.25);
\draw[bmod] (0.75, 0) -- (0.75, 0.25) --(0,1.25);
\btoken{0, 1.25}{east}{\mathfrak{u}};
\btoken{0.75, 1.25}{west}{m};
\btoken{0, 0.25}{east}{\mathcal{H}};
\btoken{0.75, 0.25}{west}{\mathcal{H}};
\end{tikzpicture} \ .
\end{equation*}
